# "Globals touched" ledger -- Firefox 140.12.0esr, PRE-ADDITION probe run.
# CHECKED-IN EVIDENCE for the one global P1.6.4 added to the v0 set.
#
# This is the raw, unedited output of `vitrin-shim --globals-log` from a run
# with `wl_subcompositor` REMOVED from the v0 set and armed as a probe
# instead -- i.e. the state the shim was in when the addition was argued for.
# It is the file that `globals-demand: interface=wl_subcompositor` actually
# lives in, and it is what src/globals.c cites.
#
# WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE FROM THE MAIN LEDGER.
# globals-touched-firefox-140.12.0esr.log is a run of the shim AS IT SHIPS, so
# wl_subcompositor appears there only as `class=v0` offers and binds: a probe
# is never created for an interface already in the contract (ledger.c,
# in_v0_contract -- advertising one interface twice, once real and once inert,
# lets the app bind the inert copy and measures a browser strictly worse than
# the real one). A post-addition log therefore CANNOT contain the demand line
# that justified the addition, and citing it for one was the defect this file
# fixes: the criterion is "every stub addition traces to a log entry", and the
# entry has to exist somewhere.
#
# THE TWO LINES THAT MATTER are at seq=15 and seq=22 below. They are the app
# stating, on the wire, that it went looking for an interface the v0 set did
# not provide -- twice, from two separate connections, which is the detail
# firefox.md reports as "from GDK and from Firefox's own display code". Read
# them next to their neighbours: seq=15 sits with `wl_compositor` v3 (GDK's
# bind) and seq=22 with `wl_compositor` v4 + `wl_seat` v8 (nsWaylandDisplay's).
#
# HOW TO REGENERATE (the shim has no flag for this on purpose -- suppressing a
# real global is not something a realm should be able to ask for, so it is a
# two-line source edit):
#
#   1. src/globals.c: comment out the `wlr_subcompositor_create(s->display)`
#      block in vitrin_create_globals().
#   2. src/ledger.c: delete the `"wl_subcompositor",` row from
#      vitrin_v0_contract[].
#   3. meson compile -C shim/build
#   4. Run the command in the header of
#      globals-touched-firefox-140.12.0esr.log, but with
#      `--probe-globals=wl_subcompositor` in place of `--probe-globals`.
#   5. Revert both edits.
#
# WHAT THE SAME BUILD DOES WITHOUT EVEN THE PROBE (step 4 with no
# --probe-globals at all), which is the other half of the bisection:
#
#   firefox exit status 139 (SIGSEGV), core dumped
#   0 windows mapped, 1 commit forwarded
#
# and with the probe armed, as recorded below: window mapped, 3 commits -- far
# short of the ~57 the shipping build forwards, because a probe is INERT and
# Firefox's content subsurface never composites. That gap is why the fix was
# `wlr_subcompositor_create` and not a stub. The full argument, including why
# a subsurface grants nothing across the realm boundary, is in src/globals.c
# and firefox.md section "The addition: wl_subcompositor".
#
# Produced 2026-07-19, wlroots 0.19.3, headless + pixman, no GPU, no network.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
